{"details":{"evidence_match":{"method":"no_contiguous_match","original_passage_span":null,"passage_byte_start":null,"proposed_evidence":"The Orion Nebula can be seen as a fuzzy patch in Orion's sword, hanging below the famous belt.","proposed_evidence_chars":94},"initial_reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","initial_status":"accepted","model_output_excerpt":"{\n  \"claim\": {\n    \"subject\": \"The Orion Nebula\",\n    \"relation\": \"is located in\",\n    \"object\": \"the constellation Orion\",\n    \"evidence_text\": \"The Orion Nebula can be seen as a fuzzy patch in Orion's sword, hanging below the famous belt.\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.98,\n    \"question_relevance\": \"direct\",\n    \"valid_from\": null,\n    \"valid_until\": null\n  }\n}","question":"The Orion Nebula is located in the constellation Orion","reason":"AI semantic entailment confirmed against original source quotation","relevance":"direct","review_guidance":null,"selected_passage_chars":1404,"selected_passage_excerpt":"# Getting to Know Orion: The Great Nebula\n\nArticle January 17, 2026\nImage\nThe Orion Nebula can be seen as a fuzzy patch in Orion’s sword, hanging below the famous belt. Credit: Stellarium\nThe Orion Nebula can be seen as a fuzzy patch in Orion’s sword, hanging below the famous belt. Credit: Stellarium\n\nQuick, what’s the nearest large star-forming region to Earth? If you don’t have that factoid ready to pull out of your back pocket, that’s hardly surprising. But this is the third in my miniseries of posts about the part of the sky occupied by the constellation Orion (here’s part 1 and part 2), so you can probably guess the answer lies somewhere in that area.\n\nAnd if you’re starting to think about nebulas in Orion, there’s one you’re more likely to be thinking about first. Nebulas can have beautiful and creative names, but not this one, alas. You might know it by its rather clinical Messier catalog designation, M42. You *probably* know it by its most well-known title, the Orion Nebula. If you’re slightly pretentious you might like to refer to it by its older label, the Great Nebula in Orion, and who am I to fault you for wanting to sound fancy?\n\nEither way, this massive star-formation region is close enough, big enough, and bright enough to be one of the few nebulas visible to the naked eye, and it just so happens to be in our buddy Orion. So let’s deep dive into this stellar nursery.","selected_passage_truncated":false,"semantic_support":{"evidence_text":"Either way, this massive star-formation region is close enough, big enough, and bright enough to be one of the few nebulas visible to the naked eye, and it just so happens to be in our buddy Orion.","model_verdict":"entailed","object":"the constellation Orion","reason":"The passage explicitly states the Orion Nebula is in our buddy Orion, confirming the relation.","relation":"is located in","stance_override":null,"subject":"The Orion Nebula","valid_from":null,"valid_until":null,"verdict":"entailed"},"source_title":"Getting to Know Orion: The Great Nebula","status":"accepted"},"event":"scholar.extraction_decision","ts_unix_ms":1791553861690}
